<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II, Elector of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1413–1471</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Frederick Irontooth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II, called Irontooth, was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from 1440 to 1470, son of Frederick I. He broke the independence of the twin towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colln">Cölln</a> in 1448 and began a castle on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spree">Spree</a> that became the Hohenzollern residence. He also bought back the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neumark">Neumark</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in 1455, and abdicated in favour of his brother Albert <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="Frederick II, Elector of Brandenburg" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_01_203_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
